0330: sweet_usb: data path v2 (one owner per endpoint, no HWO reclaim, no printf, non-cacheable DMA), boot-arg sweetusb_dp=2

A second data path for the CDC-ECM gadget, selected with sweetusb_dp=2 (in this patch the default stays the
old path; 0332 changes it). With any other value only a few `if (ud_dp)` branches and an unused sysctl are
added. Boot and PHY init, ep0 enumeration and the ECM descriptors are not changed.

- Only the USB thread touches the controller; ud_if_output queues the mbuf and wakes it (ENOBUFS when the
  queue is full or the gadget is not configured).
- One state per data endpoint (IDLE/STARTED/ENDING). STARTED ends only with an XferComplete whose TRB has
  HWO=0, or with an End Transfer that completed plus 1 ms with the event buffer drained (Linux
  51f1954ad853, gadget.c 3636-3649). A TRB or buffer is written only in IDLE.
- A refused Start keeps the staged frame, prints nothing, latches a snapshot and is followed by End
  Transfer (ForceRM) with the index the refusal reports (gadget.c 1653-1660; f7ac582effc6).
- GUCTL2[14] RST_ACTBITLATER when GSNPSID >= 3.10a; endpoint commands spin on mach_absolute_time (delay()
  blocks in this port), never with ud.lock held; GUSB2PHYCFG SUSPHY/ENBLSLPM kept clear for each command.
- Data TRBs at 0x1400/0x1440/0x1480, one per 64-byte line; the DMA area is mapped Normal non-cacheable
  (VM_WIMG_WCOMB), as arm64 Linux maps dma_alloc_coherent. boot-arg sweetusb_dpnc=0 keeps it cacheable with
  clean+invalidate per line.
- Bus reset: ep0 first, End Transfer for every STARTED endpoint, waited for, then ClearStall.
- GEVNTCOUNT & 0xfffc; no printf on the data path. Counters, End Transfer latency and latched snapshots of
  every anomaly are in sysctl kern.sweet_usb_dp.

Measured with sweetusb_dp=2 (one boot): 20 copies of 30 MB over SSH, 10 each way, all intact (SHA-256 on
both ends); after ~660 MB kern.sweet_usb_dp reads start ok 1099317, refused 0, timeout 0, noevt 0. The
same kind of copy on the old path stopped the link after 192 KiB (n=1).

